# worxboard ZMK module options (zephyr/module.yml -> kconfig: firmware/zmk/Kconfig)

config WORXBOARD_STATUS_SCREEN
    bool "worxboard status screen (both halves)"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_DISPLAY_STATUS_SCREEN_CUSTOM
    depends on BOARD_WORXBOARD_LEFT || BOARD_WORXBOARD_RIGHT || BOARD_WORXBOARD2_LEFT || BOARD_WORXBOARD2_RIGHT
    select LV_USE_LABEL
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_12
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_10
    help
      Portrait 32 x 128 screen for the 0.91" SSD1306 OLED (design.md §11.6). Central: logo, USB
      state, active layer and the Caps/Num/Scroll lock column. Peripheral: logo, the forwarded
      lock column and a static "wired" label. Uses no BLE or battery symbols.

choice WORXBOARD_DISPLAY_ROTATION
    prompt "worxboard display orientation"
    default WORXBOARD_DISPLAY_ROTATION_90
    depends on ZMK_DISPLAY
    depends on BOARD_WORXBOARD_LEFT || BOARD_WORXBOARD_RIGHT || BOARD_WORXBOARD2_LEFT || BOARD_WORXBOARD2_RIGHT
    help
      The 0.91" SSD1306 OLED (128 x 32) stands upright, so both halves lay their screen out
      portrait, 32 x 128, and src/worx_display_rotation.c turns it onto the panel.

config WORXBOARD_DISPLAY_ROTATION_90
    bool "Portrait, J3 header at the back (rev A mounting)"
    help
      LVGL LV_DISPLAY_ROTATION_90: the module's header points away from the user, as J3 holds it
      on both rev A boards. Assumes panel pixel (0, 0) is the top-left corner of the module seen
      glass up with its header on the left (not yet checked on hardware).

config WORXBOARD_DISPLAY_ROTATION_270
    bool "Portrait, turned 180 degrees from the rev A setting"
    help
      LVGL LV_DISPLAY_ROTATION_270. Use it if both screens come out upside down: the module's
      pixel (0, 0) is then at the other end from the one rev A assumes.

endchoice
